  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Kappa Canis Majoris",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Canis Major",
    "summary": "Kappa Canis Majoris is a solitary, blue-white hued star in the constellation Canis Major. Its name is a Bayer designation that is Latinized from κ Canis Majoris, and abbreviated Kappa CMa or κ CMa. This star is visible to the naked eye with an apparent visual magnitude of +3.87. Based upon an annual parallax shift of 7.70 mas as seen from Earth, this star is located about 660 light years from the Sun. It is receding from the Sun with a line of sight velocity of +14 km/s.",
